{"step_index":466,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:09:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-18T08:09:05-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-18T08:09:05-06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/djtwo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/56930dde-d49e-4d64-b3a0-ddf3ad4cb3e8/scratch/worship_utf8.txt`\nTotal Lines: 271\nTotal Bytes: 23691\nShowing lines 1 to 140\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: [00:00 -> 00:07] He's the same unchanging Jesus, the same unchanging Jesus as He was when He walked on this earth.\r\n2: [00:07 -> 00:09] So is He today.\r\n3: [00:09 -> 00:12] So this morning the invitation is to come to Him with a song of praise.\r\n4: [00:12 -> 00:18] And if you need to come to the Lord for some need, some burden, some trial that you're going through,\r\n5: [00:18 -> 00:19] you can come to Him this morning.\r\n6: [00:19 -> 00:26] He's the same Jesus to whom the woman caught in adultery came, to whom Jesus said,\r\n7: [00:26 -> 00:32] go and sin no more. He's the same Jesus that looked at Peter after He had failed.\r\n8: [00:32 -> 00:37] And He's the same Jesus that can lift us up out of the miree clay this morning, out of the pit,\r\n9: [00:37 -> 00:39] and make our footsteps firm.\r\n10: [00:39 -> 00:46] So as we sing, if we come with a need in our hearts, some void, some vacuum,\r\n11: [00:46 -> 00:51] we can come to our Lord and Savior. He's the same unchanging Jesus that sing.\r\n12: [00:54 -> 01:00] Ooh, glory, it's to God He has lived in me, He has lived in me.\r\n13: [01:00 -> 01:05] He reached out.\r\n14: [01:05 -> 01:45] He reached out and said, and He lived in me.\r\n15: [01:45 -> 01:49] And that's why I love Him so.\r\n16: [01:49 -> 02:32] Mother, so rather so, is the same Jesus unchanging Jesus.\r\n17: [02:32 -> 02:39] An unchanging Jesus is the same unchanging Jesus.\r\n18: [02:39 -> 02:43] Jesus is true, He journeyed to you.\r\n19: [02:43 -> 02:47] He is the same unchanging Jesus.\r\n20: [02:47 -> 02:49] An unchanging Je\n<truncated 7758 bytes>\nto stay here for longer, we will.\r\n126: [25:42 -> 25:48] If it's for more fellowship downstairs or out in the park, we'll continue that. But we're a people\r\n127: [25:48 -> 25:54] who are seeking to walk with the Lord and His people all the time, not just for an hour on Sunday\r\n128: [25:54 -> 26:00] morning. Sadly, the devil has turned much of Christendom into that kind of a Christian life,\r\n129: [26:00 -> 26:06] or church life, where you segment the kingdom of heaven into one or one and a half hours on a Sunday\r\n130: [26:06 -> 26:12] morning, and maybe a Wednesday Bible study or a Friday Bible study. And the rest of your life,\r\n131: [26:12 -> 26:20] you live for yourself. That's not Christianity. And so we enjoy being together and thankful that the\r\n132: [26:20 -> 26:25] Lord has placed us in a church where we are excited to be together. I'm certainly excited to be\r\n133: [26:25 -> 26:31] here. We sing, He is the glory and the lifter of our heads. That means that if there's any burden\r\n134: [26:31 -> 26:39] you're carrying, anything that causes your head to hang down. It's look to Jesus and He is the glory\r\n135: [26:39 -> 26:44] and the lifter of our heads. He's done that for me already this morning. I hope you experience that\r\n136: [26:44 -> 26:49] during the time of singing. If you were singing to Christ and you recognized His presence here, I believe\r\n137: [26:50 -> 26:57] He has lifted your head. May that be so. Welcome to all of you and to our visitors online as well.\r\n138: [26:57 -> 27:04] We're thankful that many of you chose to join us quite regularly. Most of you, we have never gotten\r\n139: [27:04 -> 27:11] to meet in person, but we're aware that there are God's people who love Him first of all or part of\r\n140: [27:11 -> 27:17] His family, but also are seeking to go this narrow way as we are and emphasize the things that\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
